---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageIntro from "../../components/PageIntro.astro";

const title = "Retired tools";
const description =
  "Historical source for the diagnostics and agent prompt packs retired on September 26, 2026, and the ethics scorecard retired on October 1.";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  breadcrumbItems={[
    { name: "Home", url: "/" },
    { name: "Diagnostics", url: "/diagnostics" },
    { name: title, url: "/archive/retired-tools" },
  ]}
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="Archive"
    title={title}
    description={description}
    anchorLinks={[]}
  />
  <section class="stack-md" aria-labelledby="retirement-reason">
    <h2 id="retirement-reason">Why these tools were retired</h2>
    <p>
      The System Auditor reviewed prompt text with regular expressions. Its
      score could not establish whether an institution could correct a decision.
      The Governance Gap Score duplicated the Delegation Audit with fewer
      questions. Both now redirect to the <a
        href="/diagnostics/delegation-audit">Delegation Audit</a
      >, which records self-reported answers and does not verify them.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Capacity Forecaster, Maintenance Simulator, and Maintenance Debt
      Calculator modeled general operational planning. Their URLs now redirect
      to
      <a href="/diagnostics">Diagnostics</a>. The general agent prompt packs and
      installation interface are also retired.
    </p>
    <p>
      The Ethics Audit Scorecard was retired on October 1, 2026. It scored
      transparency, accountability, fairness, privacy, sustainability, and power.
      That is a general ethics checklist, not the six safeguards this site
      measures. Its URL now opens the <a href="/#self-test">self-test</a>, which
      asks one question for each safeguard. Its source remains in the public
      repository's history.
    </p>
    <p>
      These materials remain available for historical reference. They are not
      maintained tools or evidence that a deployment has effective corrective
      authority. The <a href="/diagnostics/record-conformance"
        >Record Conformance Checker</a
      >
      remains available to check specific properties of a record stream.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="stack-md" aria-labelledby="historical-source">
    <h2 id="historical-source">Historical source and downloads</h2>
    <p>
      The source archive preserves the retired applications, tests, prompt
      packs, and their original catalogue entries at commit
      <code>c1b3f00fd0b2e9c589f45baeb6a43d0609d72142</code>. It also includes
      glossary and mechanism snapshots so removed references can be interpreted
      in their original context.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="/archive/retired-tools/source.tar.gz" download
          >Download source archive</a
        >
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="/archive/retired-tools/manifest.json"
          >Archive manifest and SHA-256 checksum</a
        >
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          href="/archive/retired-tools/ethotechnics-agent-prompt-pack-v1.0.0.md"
          download>Historical prompt pack v1.0.0</a
        >
      </li>
      <li>
        <a
          href="/archive/retired-tools/ethotechnics-agent-prompt-pack-v1.1.0.md"
          download>Historical prompt pack v1.1.0</a
        >
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
